Over these capped runs the repaired rules took 0.02% more nodes. That is a hint, not a cost measurement; item 04 measures cost. New tests: `pathwidth_solver/tests/test_repaired_rules.py` (8 tests), and `test_identity_mosp.py` now runs under both settings.

**No certified value changed and no false refutation turned up.** One thing for items 06–08: the certificate emitter in `learning/search_certificate.py` still models only the published rules, so anything compared against it needs the flag off. PROGRESS.md is updated (3/10) and the item is marked `[x]`. Nothing was committed and nothing was written to `solutions/`.

